    "text": "To determine how many miles Wendy drove on the third day, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the total miles driven over the three days.\n2. Subtract the miles driven on the first and second days from the total miles.\n\nThe total miles driven over the three days is given as 493 miles. Wendy drove 125 miles on the first day and 223 miles on the second day. Let's denote the miles driven on the third day as \\( x \\).\n\nThe equation representing the total miles driven is:\n\\[ 125 + 223 + x = 493 \\]\n\nFirst, we add the miles driven on the first and second days:\n\\[ 125 + 223 = 348 \\]\n\nNow, we substitute this sum back into the equation:\n\\[ 348 + x = 493 \\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we subtract 348 from both sides of the equation:\n\\[ x = 493 - 348 \\]\n\\[ x = 145 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of miles Wendy drove on the third day is \\(\\boxed{145}\\).",
